---
import { currentFocus } from "../data/currentFocus";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const updatedDate = new Date(`${currentFocus.updatedAt}T00:00:00Z`);
const updatedMonth = new Intl.DateTimeFormat("en-US", {
  month: "long",
  year: "numeric",
  timeZone: "UTC",
}).format(updatedDate);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Paula Grangeiro's path from senior software engineer to hands-on engineering manager."
>
  <div class="space-y-10">
    <header class="space-y-3 border-b border-hairline pb-6">
      <span class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-terracotta">
        BIOGRAPHY & PHILOSOPHY
      </span>
      <h1 class="max-w-3xl font-editorial text-3xl font-bold text-ink sm:text-4xl">
        From Software Engineer to hands-on Engineering Manager
      </h1>
    </header>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 md:grid-cols-3">
      <div class="space-y-6 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink md:col-span-2">
        <p>
          Over the last decade, I've journeyed from building distributed systems
          and backend software as an IC to guiding engineering teams as an
          Engineering Manager.
        </p>
        <p>
          I believe the most effective engineering managers in the AI era
          maintain deep technical empathy. When coding agents accelerate
          implementation, engineering leadership isn't about managing backlog
          status - it's about mentoring engineers, setting architectural
          standards, and fostering team psychological safety.
        </p>

        <section
          aria-labelledby="current-focus"
          class="space-y-4 rounded-2xl border border-[#333] bg-ink p-6 text-paper shadow-md"
        >
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3 border-b border-[#333] pb-3">
            <h2
              class="font-mono text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-terracotta-on-dark"
              id="current-focus"
            >
              Current Focus
            </h2>
            <time
              class="font-mono text-[10px] text-muted-light"
              datetime={currentFocus.updatedAt}
            >
              Updated {updatedMonth}
            </time>
          </div>
          <div class="grid gap-4 font-mono text-xs text-sand sm:grid-cols-2 sm:text-sm">
            <div class="space-y-1">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-terracotta-on-dark">Building</h3>
              <p class="leading-relaxed text-muted-light">
                {currentFocus.building}
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="space-y-1">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-terracotta-on-dark">
                Leading &amp; Mentoring
              </h3>
              <p class="leading-relaxed text-muted-light">
                {currentFocus.leadingAndMentoring}
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="space-y-1">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-terracotta-on-dark">Reading</h3>
              <ul class="space-y-1 text-muted-light">
                {currentFocus.reading.map(({ title }) => (
                  <li>
                    <em>{title}</em>
                  </li>
                ))}
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <h2 class="pt-2 font-editorial text-xl font-bold text-ink">
          Core beliefs I lead by
        </h2>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          <section class="rounded-xl border border-hairline bg-sand p-4">
            <h3 class="font-mono text-sm font-bold text-terracotta">
              1. Lead by example
            </h3>
            <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-muted">
              Know the work before you delegate it. When ambiguity arises, help
              the team find a path forward.
            </p>
          </section>
          <section class="rounded-xl border border-hairline bg-sand p-4">
            <h3 class="font-mono text-sm font-bold text-terracotta">
              2. AI multiplies leverage, not quality
            </h3>
            <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-muted">
              AI speeds up output, not judgment. Teach teams to use it well and
              keep architectural boundaries clear.
            </p>
          </section>
          <section class="rounded-xl border border-hairline bg-sand p-4">
            <h3 class="font-mono text-sm font-bold text-terracotta">
              3. Silence isn't feedback
            </h3>
            <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-muted">
              Give feedback early and specifically. People deserve to know
              what to keep doing and what to change.
            </p>
          </section>
        </div>
      </div>

      <aside class="h-fit space-y-4 rounded-2xl border border-hairline bg-sand p-6">
        <h2 class="font-mono text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-terracotta">
          Connect & Socials
        </h2>
        <nav aria-label="Social profiles" class="space-y-3 font-mono text-sm">
          <a
            class="flex items-start gap-3 text-ink hover:text-terracotta"
            href="https://github.com/pgrangeiro"
            rel="noreferrer"
            target="_blank"
          >
            <i
              aria-hidden="true"
              class="bi bi-github mt-0.5 shrink-0 text-xl leading-none"
            ></i>
            <span>GitHub (@pgrangeiro)</span>
          </a>
          <a
            class="flex items-start gap-3 text-ink hover:text-terracotta"
            href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/paulagrangeiro/"
            rel="noreferrer"
            target="_blank"
          >
            <i
              aria-hidden="true"
              class="bi bi-linkedin mt-0.5 shrink-0 text-xl leading-none"
            ></i>
            <span>LinkedIn (/in/paulagrangeiro)</span>
          </a>
        </nav>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
